From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: prefer an available narrower channel before MLD DFS restart

A 160 MHz radar event can leave no immediately usable 160 MHz target.
The existing fallback first chooses a CAC-required channel at that width,
disables the interface and tears down the MLD station even when a legal
80 MHz target is available. Prefer available narrower widths for an MLD
so the existing per-link CSA path can preserve the surviving links.

Keep ETSI uniform-spreading selection and legacy AP behavior unchanged.
Use the existing regulatory/DFS filter and restore the original width
before the original CAC/NOP fallback when no available target exists.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/dfs.c
+++ b/src/ap/dfs.c
@@ -1482,6 +1482,25 @@
 					&oper_centr_freq_seg1_idx,
 					channel_type);
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	/* Avoid restarting an MLD for CAC when a narrower channel is ready. */
+	if (!channel && channel_type == DFS_AVAILABLE &&
+	    iface->bss[0]->conf->mld_ap) {
+		int width = current_vht_oper_chwidth;
+
+		while (!channel && width > CONF_OPER_CHWIDTH_USE_HT) {
+			hostapd_set_oper_chwidth(iface->conf, --width);
+			channel = dfs_get_valid_channel(iface, &secondary_channel,
+						&oper_centr_freq_seg0_idx,
+						&oper_centr_freq_seg1_idx,
+						DFS_AVAILABLE);
+		}
+		if (!channel)
+			hostapd_set_oper_chwidth(iface->conf,
+						current_vht_oper_chwidth);
+	}
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+
 	if (!channel) {
 		/*
